# Beat The Hazard — results service (optional)
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in to connect the game to a Supabase project.
# Leave them unset and the game behaves exactly as it always has: accounts and
# results stay on the device and the supervisor page says there is no service.
#
# Both values are public. The anon key is designed to ship inside a web page,
# and the database's row level security is what protects the data: a trainee
# can write and read only their own rows, an admin can read everything and
# write nothing, and a stored round cannot be edited by anyone.
#
# The service role key is the secret one. It is never used here and must never
# be committed: it bypasses every policy above.
#
# Where to find these: Supabase dashboard → Settings → API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
